0,Uru people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uru_people,"The Uru or Uros (Uru: Qhas Qut suñi) are an indigenous people of Bolivia and Peru. They live on a still-growing group of about 120 self-fashioned floating islands in Lake Titicaca near Puno. They form three main groups: the Uru-Chipaya, Uru-Murato, and Uru-Iruito.",Uru,Chipaya-Uru
1,Uru-ChipayaUru-Chipaya - DOBES,https://dobes.mpi.nl/projects/uru-chipaya/,Uru-Chipaya media. Access and Registration.Uru-Chipaya is the linguistic term for the language varieties originally spoken by the Urus who constitute some small ethnic groups inhabiting the Altiplano region of Bolivia and Peru.,Uru,Chipaya-Uru
2,"Uru - Songs, Events and Music Stats | Viberate.com",https://www.viberate.com/artist/uru-762/,"In general, Uru's music serves as a showcase for her musical talent and inventiveness. Her ability to write music that is both uplifting and emotionally resonant is evidence of her commitment to her profession.The Uru-Chipaya, Uru-Murato, and Uru-Iruito are their three primary groups.",Uru,Chipaya-Uru
